Subject: [PATCH 1/2] refactor(rolling): the tray one export per file, words
 per kind, toasts, small components, dice entry

The tray, toasts, menus and dice entry: R-b's lane (round.md R1.2.8-R1.2.11, R1.2.12b). RollTray and
the twenty components it held each have a file of their own under features/rolling/components/roll-tray/, with
BADGES and BADGE_ICONS in the folder's constants.ts and its small pure helpers in its utils.ts.
The tray's words are in utils/tray-words.ts, the Gamemaster's in utils/gm-words.ts, and briefOf
and its pieces stay in utils/brief.ts. The seven way-word copies read one wayWords, and the four
status lines are one StatusLine. breakdown goes by kind. usedWords, TableMark, gmLine, tableLine
and briefOf are each 15 or less. gmShape reads ROLL_KIND_INFO, and NOT_MADE comes from
constants/lifecycle. Strings, class order, spans and useId order are copied, never retyped.

Toasts: popToasts is split into four steps, the same reads and writes in the same order. Toast
and Badge have their own files. The turn's foot comes through useTurnToastFoot. useToastSetting
and useToastTop stay in hooks/use-roll-toasts, where the sheet and the table import them (a
Phase 4 item). Small components: ModifyDamage has its own file in modify-roll/, and criticalHint
and labelsFor are in utils/damage-words.ts. useD20Rolls, useDamageMenu and useDiceEntry are
.ts hooks. Each returns createElement of its own dialogs component (d20-dialogs.tsx,
damage-dialogs.tsx, dice-entry-dialogs.tsx), which holds the JSX it used to return. That adds
one component level and no DOM node. rollOf (utils/sheet-rolls.ts) builds the three
check-and-save bodies with the same keys in the same order. DiceKey and Asked are in
dice-entry/types.ts. The prop types left the .tsx files.

React hooks findings: floating-ui's ref setters are taken out of `refs` first (choice-menu,
rolls-button). The dice dialog's scroll goes through a module function. use-roll-toasts' clock
read after commit keeps its timing, so it has one line disable with its reason.

L1 on this tree: jest 305 suites, 9,689 tests, 0 red; typegen and tsc clean; eslint 0 errors,
624 warnings (640 after the tray split). In this lane's files the warnings went from 41 at
a2332a2 to 4: rule (a) .tsx files 6 to 0, named types in .tsx 6 to 0, cognitive complexity over
15 7 to 0, and react-hooks findings 4 to 0 (one line disable). The 4 left are exported types in
tray-words.ts and roll-toasts.ts, which belong in features/rolling/types.ts (R-a's file), so they
are a Phase 4 item. Gates 1-12 ok, C1-C9 unchanged, 3 cycle groups as before. No test file was
split, and the one test change is an import line.

